                "word": "parenx",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "2eb8d4d1-a07b-415f-9aef-380f4d5d8865",
                        "entry_id": "65c45762-ba95-3d12-8c76-a0509c07d341",
                        "tags": [
                            "singular"
                        ],
                        "form": "parenz"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "8049ba10-0f03-3e40-8f97-27c494e0d95e",
                        "entry_id": "65c45762-ba95-3d12-8c76-a0509c07d341",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Individu quel que soit son genre, qui a pris le rôle et la responsabilité parentale dans la vie d’un·e enfant."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "Variations diaéthiques"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "5b3ba935-a4ff-405e-9549-16d741cfdd49",
                                "sense_id": "8049ba10-0f03-3e40-8f97-27c494e0d95e",
                                "text": "Dans le premier cas, les notions de père et de mère renvoient selon nous au sexe (biologique) du parenx*. En effet, l’établissement de la filiation dépend d’éléments biologiques traditionnellement associés au sexe (disposer d’un utérus pour la personne accouchant ou disposer de spermatozoïdes pour lu* conjoinx* mariæ*, présumæ* être père)."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "65b79eb2-afa1-484a-99ff-4ced0519811c",
                                "sense_id": "8049ba10-0f03-3e40-8f97-27c494e0d95e",
                                "text": "On laissera de côté ici les problèmes de conventionalité liés à des règles à la portée incertaine, telle par exemple la possibilité pour les mineurz représentæs d’accéder au changement, ou encore la possibilité, dans l’intérêt de l’enfant et de ses parenz*, d’établir leur filiation en fonction du sexe (biologique) du parenx et non de son genre."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "82c9c139-0a70-4d29-b5ba-9f8a1944365a",
                        "source_entry_id": "65c45762-ba95-3d12-8c76-a0509c07d341",
                        "source_sense_id": "8049ba10-0f03-3e40-8f97-27c494e0d95e",
                        "target_lang_word": "parent",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "parent",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "04a91bd6-8b71-3784-8861-024d9129b4aa",
                                        "entry_id": "f6fbc730-ee8c-3fb0-8e90-e72d220fbc2b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A person who raises a child (which they have made, adopted, fostered, taken as their own, etc.)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "in-plural",
                                            "often"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "bef116cd-7f24-429d-aa59-5a666971c9bf",
                                                "sense_id": "04a91bd6-8b71-3784-8861-024d9129b4aa",
                                                "text": "After both her parents were killed in a forest fire, Sonia was adopted by her aunt and uncle."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "979b52d7-075e-482f-8772-5826288d8ece",
                                                "sense_id": "04a91bd6-8b71-3784-8861-024d9129b4aa",
                                                "text": "my trust / Like a good parent, did beget of him / A falsehood in it's contrarie, as great / As my trust was, which had indeede no limit, / A confidence sans bound."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fdc2dc58-86d3-40f9-be70-3a2f75064521",
                                                "sense_id": "04a91bd6-8b71-3784-8861-024d9129b4aa",
                                                "text": "And they asked them, saying, Is this your son, who ye say was born blind? how then doth he now see? His parents answered them and said, We know that this is our son, and that he was born blind […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5d35c96d-0a5f-49ad-b3c9-1543d1253d20",
                                                "sense_id": "04a91bd6-8b71-3784-8861-024d9129b4aa",
                                                "text": "The NHS is naturally pro-immunisation, reassuring parents that their babies can easily cope with these jabs."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f9c74def-7f71-401d-9923-f2c75f6e37f7",
                                                "sense_id": "04a91bd6-8b71-3784-8861-024d9129b4aa",
                                                "text": "It is time the international community faced the reality: we have an unmanageable, unfair, distortionary global tax regime. […] It is the starving of the public sector which has been pivotal in America no longer being the land of opportunity – with a child's life prospects more dependent on the income and education of its parents than in other advanced countries."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "325b9ca7-e311-307e-82cf-538cef005499",
                                        "entry_id": "f6fbc730-ee8c-3fb0-8e90-e72d220fbc2b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A person who has had a baby; this person in relation to their child or children."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "in-plural",
                                            "often"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2ba1662b-8878-3aae-95e6-9d8ad305604b",
                                        "entry_id": "f6fbc730-ee8c-3fb0-8e90-e72d220fbc2b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A surrogate parent."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "cec1f565-ce51-3e5d-971f-17f0aac43451",
                                        "entry_id": "f6fbc730-ee8c-3fb0-8e90-e72d220fbc2b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A third person who has provided DNA samples in an IVF procedure in order to alter faulty genetic material."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
